    "created_at": "2016-01-20T16:15:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-20T16:15:17Z",
    "body": "The representation of dates is not just for representing the current time. It is for representing any date that could ever occur in a document, including e.g. dates in sci-fi novels or articles about the formation of the Earth.\n\nIf your particular application does not deal with these scenarios, it's perfectly all right to add validation to it to disallow years after 9999, or after 2016, or any other such restriction. The HTML Standard provides plenty of validation tools you can use such as setCustomValidity().\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/173254191/reactions",
