    "created_at": "2016-01-20T17:57:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-20T17:57:43Z",
    "body": "> articles about the formation of the Earth.\n\nThis isn't supported since negative years are not allowed. The lower limit is somewhat arbitrary but convenient syntax-wise. And since it's non-trivial to translate moments in time that long ago into the Gregorian calendar, it's not so useful to mark up anyway. I suppose the same argument could be made for time far in the future, too, though.\n\nWhat actual problem does this cause, though? Is it not a problem that year 3000+ is allowed? It seems to me the argument in OP applies equally to 3000+ or many other arbitrary maxes.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
